  "id": "payoff-matrix",
  "term": "payoff matrix",
  "definition": "A payoff matrix is a 2-by-2 table used in a game to determine the score each player receives from the combination of both players’ choices. In the Prisoner’s Dilemma described here, it specifies the outcomes for cooperation or betrayal by each player.",
